m-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The KLR algebra `R(Γ)` categorifies U⁻_q(g) where `g = g(Γ)`\n(opaque marker for Khovanov-Lauda-Rouquier theorem). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRCategorifiesNegativeHalfUqg.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRCategorifiesNegativeHalfUqg.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRCategorifiesNegativeHalfUqg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRCategorifiesNegativeHalfUqg","kind":"class","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L67-L72","doc":"Conditional class axiomatising the KLR ↔ U⁻_q(g) categorification.\nNEAR-MATCH tier; instance not constructed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.trivialQuiver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.trivialQuiver","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The **trivial quiver**: one vertex, no edges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRAlgebra.klr_structure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRAlgebra.klr_structure","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L50-L50","doc":"KLR algebra structure exists for `A` over `R` (opaque marker for\nthe open derivation; instance gates the categorical promotion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRAlgebra","kind":"class","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L44-L50","doc":"A **KLR algebra** over a quiver `Γ` is an `R`-algebra `A` with\ngenerators `idem`, `dot`, `crossing` satisfying the KLR relations.\nCaptured here as an opaque type-class for downstream consumers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver.adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver.adj","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Adjacency multiplicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver.I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver.I","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The vertex type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KLRQuiver","kind":"structure","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KLRAlgebraBasic.lean#L34-L42","doc":"A **quiver** `Γ` for the KLR algebra: a type of vertices `I`\ntogether with an adjacency map `adj : I → I → ℕ` (multiplicity of\nedges). For the standard simply-laced case all multiplicities are\n0 or 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}